A||N||3||SloPonti||need help on how to remove panels in the interior!!||||6||
Z||000000||SloPonti||05-08-2000||11:47 PM||||i am getting the rear window tinted in my fiero and i need to remove the headliner so the guy can get the tint to cover the whole window! how do i remove the back side panels? also how do i remove the panels above the doors that run along the sides of the winshield?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||6
Z||000001||rcn491||05-09-2000||12:40 AM||||First remove the plastic trim along the bottom of door. This will expose a sheet metal screw on bottom of rear panel.Remove seat belt bolts. (use Torx head tool). Rear speakers may also need to be removed. Remove stop light cover. Trim on top of door opening is held on by internal plastic clip that will break if your not careful. This should alow top rear of headliner to drop down enough to install trim. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||05-09-2000||10:40 AM||||You don't have to mess with the speakers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jfuredy||05-09-2000||01:22 PM||||I would recommend removing the passenger's side trim components.  You only need to remove the upper trim piece (the one most likely to break) on one side, and it's easier to get the bottom trim off of hte passenger's side without the parking brake lever in the way.<P>There's also a single screw in the door jam that holds the rear panels in place.<P>Good luck,<BR>Joe Furedy||||reg||1
